SUMMARY: Opening Reception: Perfectly Imperfect by Cameron Story
DESCRIPTION:Perfectly Imperfect\n\nBy Featured Artist Cameron Story at Us
 her Gallery\n\nThis exhibition focuses on the power of imperfection.\n\nJ
 oin us for the opening reception of Perfectly Imperfect on May 2nd from 5
 pm to 8pm. Enjoy live music by The Hot Clams\, a spread of refreshments a
 nd wine\, and our lively community! Perfectly Imperfect will be on displa
 y at Usher Gallery from April 28th to May 31st.\n\n“The concept of perfec
 tion can drive us or paralyze us\, but either way\, we are trying to live
  up to something that doesn’t truly exist. The fear of not achieving perf
 ection often stops us before we even begin. Think about how often you’ve 
 allowed this idea to intercept your desire to try something new or expres
 s yourself differently for fear of judgment. I felt the desire to paint f
 or years before ever putting paint to canvas. Now\, through acrylic\, res
 in\, metal leaf\, and a variety of mixed media\, I’m able to push past th
 ese fears and express my most authentic self\, fully embracing that it wi
 ll not be perfect. Nor would I want it to be. If creativity is to flow fr
 eely\, it needs to be imperfect. This has allowed me to become an artist\
 , and I’m truly grateful. Whether it’s art or any other driving force in 
 our lives\, I encourage everyone to consider imperfection as a gift that 
 allows us to grow and thrive.”\n\n- Cameron Story\, Show Statement
CATEGORIES:livemusic,opening,gallery,community
